\description{
Read the files written by a run of \code{\link[=cellcoal_run]{cellcoal_run()}} (or any results folder of CellCoal), one replicate at
a time. Each reader needs its output among the options of the run: \code{-6} for the tree, \code{-1} for the
genotypes, \code{-2} for the haplotypes, read counts (\code{-C}) for the VCF and the allelic dropout of the cells.
\code{cellcoal_read()} reads all of them that the run wrote. The cells are named as in CellCoal (\code{cell0001},
..., and the healthy outgroup \code{outgcell}) or as the tips of a user tree.
}
\details{
\itemize{
\item \code{cellcoal_tree()}: the genealogy, with branch lengths in expected mutations per site.
\item \code{cellcoal_genotypes()}: the genotypes of the variable sites (file \code{snv_gen}): with allelic dropout and
genotyping error, or, with read counts, the maximum likelihood genotypes. \verb{?} is an allele lost by
dropout and \code{N} a missing genotype; with the binary alphabet, the alleles are \code{0} and \code{1}.
\item \code{cellcoal_haplotypes()}: the maternal and paternal haplotypes of the variable sites (file \code{snv_hap}).
\item \code{cellcoal_ado()}: the allelic dropout rate of every cell (file \code{ado_cells}).
\item \code{cellcoal_vcf()}: fields of the VCF, e.g. \code{GT} (called genotype), \code{DP} (depth), \code{RC} (read counts of
A, C, G, T), \code{NG} (genotype in the library, after dropout) and \code{TG} (true genotype); the header of the
VCF and the manual describe all of them. Compressed VCFs (\code{-z}) are read; BCFs (\code{--bcf}) are not.
}

A replicate without variable sites gives no rows (genotypes, haplotypes) or no sites (VCF).
